  ('89ca328a-d47e-5259-838a-c1475fc6db71', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-narrative-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Sentence 11 summarizes what the coach said. Which revision uses dialogue that best fits this moment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Daniela remembered that Coach Abernathy had said something at practice once.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-dialogue"},{"text":"\"I really love this hill,\" Daniela said to herself with a laugh.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-scene"},{"text":"Coach Abernathy's voice echoed in her head: \"Short steps on hills. Let your arms do the work.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Good luck out there,\" a stranger called from the crowd.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-moment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Coach Abernathy's voice echoed in her head: "Short steps on hills. Let your arms do the work."$q$, $q$The coach's words about short steps and arms lead directly into sentence 12, where Daniela pumps her arms and shortens her stride. The stranger's line is dialogue, but it has nothing to do with how she climbs the hill.$q$, 'draft', '487a96b0-9069-540a-ae60-fca433bf38ed')
