   $q$Which revision of sentence 8 best uses description to build tension?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Then the course turned uphill, and Daniela started thinking about lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-breaks-tension"},{"text":"Then the course turned uphill, which happens on many cross-country courses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-detail"},{"text":"Then the course turned uphill for a while, and it kept going up.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-detail"},{"text":"Then the Wall rose in front of her, steep and muddy and laced with roots.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Then the Wall rose in front of her, steep and muddy and laced with roots.$q$, $q$Naming the Wall and describing it as steep, muddy and full of roots shows the challenge Daniela faces. Saying that hills happen on many courses adds a general fact instead of building tension in this scene.$q$, 'draft', '487a96b0-9069-540a-ae60-fca433bf38ed')
