   $q$Suppose sentence 7 has been moved to its correct place. Which sentence would best replace sentence 15 as the conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"As she bent over to catch her breath, Daniela grinned, because this time the Wall had not beaten her.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Cross-country races in middle school are usually about two or three miles long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Daniela crossed the finish line in twenty-first place.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-sentence"},{"text":"The next week, Daniela's family adopted a puppy from the shelter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-unrelated-event"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As she bent over to catch her breath, Daniela grinned, because this time the Wall had not beaten her.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows Daniela's feeling after the race and connects back to the Wall named in sentence 2. Once sentence 7 is moved, the finish place has already been told, so repeating it adds nothing.$q$, 'draft', '487a96b0-9069-540a-ae60-fca433bf38ed')
