   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 by showing Tariq's feelings and connecting to the opening?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Afterward, the members of the orchestra folded up their music stands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"Backstage, Tariq's hands still trembled, but he was smiling at the solo that had once made his stomach drop.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The cello is the second largest instrument in the string family.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Afterward, Tariq felt very, very good about how everything had gone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tells-not-shows"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Backstage, Tariq's hands still trembled, but he was smiling at the solo that had once made his stomach drop.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows Tariq's emotion through his hands and smile and links to sentence 3, where his stomach dropped. Adding "very, very" still only tells the reader how he felt.$q$, 'draft', '07a8501f-fef4-5e95-8e0d-e51beaec2332')
