   $q$Which revision of sentence 4 best shows a shift in both time and setting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Similarly, we parked our car in a quiet field somewhere outside of town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comparison-not-time"},{"text":"Meanwhile, back at home, we parked our car in a field outside of town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradictory-setting"},{"text":"About an hour later, we parked in a dark field where the city lights were only a glow on the horizon.","is_correct":true},{"text":"As a result of the star map, we parked in a field outside of town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$About an hour later, we parked in a dark field where the city lights were only a glow on the horizon.$q$, $q$"About an hour later" marks the time that passed, and the dark field with a distant glow shows the new setting. "Meanwhile, back at home" contradicts the fact that they have driven out of the city.$q$, 'draft', 'a16a8458-1b5f-5b95-a034-e4a19bbd7b00')
