  ('dad92d95-f5a0-5660-96f5-8446ae7aab7a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 17 as a conclusion that reflects on the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some comets return only once every several hundred years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"We drove home, and the trip back took about an hour.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"That night I decided to become a famous scientist and win every award there is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-ending"},{"text":"On the drive home, I kept my face pressed to the window, watching a sky I had never bothered to look at before.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On the drive home, I kept my face pressed to the window, watching a sky I had never bothered to look at before.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows a believable change in the narrator, who now pays attention to the night sky. Deciding to win every award is a huge leap that the events of one night do not support.$q$, 'draft', 'a16a8458-1b5f-5b95-a034-e4a19bbd7b00')
