   $q$Sentences 7 and 8 are short and repetitive. Which revision best combines them using precise description?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He wobbled, and he wobbled, and then he wobbled some more.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repetition-no-detail"},{"text":"He wobbled because bikes are hard for young kids to balance.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"explains-instead-of-shows"},{"text":"The front wheel jerked left, then right, and his knuckles turned pale on the handlebars.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He wobbled, which is something all new riders do sometimes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-aside"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The front wheel jerked left, then right, and his knuckles turned pale on the handlebars.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows the wobbling through specific movements and Kofi's tight grip. The choice explaining that bikes are hard to balance tells a general reason instead of showing the scene.$q$, 'draft', '2f9c1c80-8172-5c78-8880-5a3902b5cacf')
