   $q$The story is told by Kofi's older sibling. Which sentence, if added after sentence 14, would break the first-person point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"My hand was still stretched out in the empty air.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pov"},{"text":"Kofi secretly thought his sibling was the best teacher ever.","is_correct":true},{"text":"I could hear his tires humming on the pavement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pov"},{"text":"I held my breath and waited for him to tip over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pov"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kofi secretly thought his sibling was the best teacher ever.$q$, $q$A first-person narrator cannot know another character's secret thoughts, so that sentence breaks the point of view. The other sentences describe what the narrator hears, sees or does, which a first-person narrator can report.$q$, 'draft', '2f9c1c80-8172-5c78-8880-5a3902b5cacf')
