   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 as a conclusion that resolves the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"His eyes went wide and he tipped into the grass, but he came up laughing. \"Again! Don't hold on this time!\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"I realized that teaching someone takes patience, and that is the lesson of this story.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"tells-moral-directly"},{"text":"Kofi got a brand new bike for his birthday the next year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-unrelated-event"},{"text":"He fell over, and then we walked the bike back home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His eyes went wide and he tipped into the grass, but he came up laughing. "Again! Don't hold on this time!"$q$, $q$The correct choice resolves Kofi's fear by showing him eager to ride without help, which contrasts with his shouting in sentence 9. The choice that states "the lesson of this story" tells the meaning outright instead of showing it.$q$, 'draft', '2f9c1c80-8172-5c78-8880-5a3902b5cacf')
